{"title":"2019 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(using_the_answer_choices)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (using the answer choices)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Faster_Solution_1)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Faster Solution 1)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution(Comprehensive🧠)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution(Comprehensive🧠)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a high school with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/9/a39b14023c98c943554d150561aacc188c4ce26d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$500$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> students, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/e/f4e4e5c6d549ce47918b94180cad5c1644d9ea88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> of the seniors play a musical instrument, while <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/e/32e5939a7bdd847ec86582225cd653c240b4abce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> of the non-seniors do not play a musical instrument. In all, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/8/4282af23ed227721fc5c07c3a27f24991cc4e04a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$46.8\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> of the students do not play a musical instrument. How many non-seniors play a musical instrument?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/c/2dce93191c3cfc083d8412854e37c09ed639cf44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 66 \\qquad\\textbf{(B) } 154 \\qquad\\textbf{(C) } 186 \\qquad\\textbf{(D) } 220 \\qquad\\textbf{(E) } 266$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"434\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/7/fd7edd3842c40dbc1e54e522917a6e07b43c92e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> of seniors do not play a musical instrument. If we denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> as the number of seniors, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/b/39beb27287fd9606cb72594254ed23d8f84d808a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{3}{5}x + \\frac{3}{10}\\cdot(500-x) = \\frac{468}{1000}\\cdot500\\]\" width=\"257\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbf60a030fd69addddedd21963193e62f2f4e54.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{3}{5}x + 150 - \\frac{3}{10}x = 234\\]\" width=\"177\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/0/ae0b9942f3104e50463964898645e3071ad35d75.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{3}{10}x = 84\\]\" width=\"72\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/1/e917d53d7f0e260365f5b83bbee0d622ee11793d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = 84\\cdot\\frac{10}{3} = 280\\]\" width=\"138\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Thus there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/e/47ef014290c26c25db4e335747340b12dbc08006.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$500-x = 220$\" width=\"110\" height=\"12\" /> non-seniors. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/2/282fdef75f579c92565cd7e0734d83ccfd38bfdc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> of the non-seniors play a musical instrument, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/c/04cef0977ce5174289db5199dd3009f63e6ce5dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$220 \\cdot \\frac{7}{10} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B) } 154}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"160\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>~IronicNinja\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of seniors, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be the number of non-seniors. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/f/c7f0504b3bfa775132523a004e290ee0d48efc5e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{3}{5}x + \\frac{3}{10}y = \\frac{468}{1000}\\cdot500 = 234\\]\" width=\"231\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Multiplying both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> gives us\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/d/eed3fa790604393aa68809319e61bca0eba6aee2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[6x + 3y = 2340\\]\" width=\"119\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/a/e7aa5b9336ea438e5c68fa1fd1d1885c89074e7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + y = 500$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"93\" height=\"16\" /> because there are 500 students in total.\n</p><p>Solving these system of equations give us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/c/bbcb8f6a3a3c3257b4bbcf9cb4c5a5d276de063a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 280$\" width=\"61\" height=\"12\" />,   <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/2/19247c32847819879cb0039f1afce2c7465a8d3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 220$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/2/282fdef75f579c92565cd7e0734d83ccfd38bfdc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> of the non-seniors play a musical instrument, the answer is simply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/2/282fdef75f579c92565cd7e0734d83ccfd38bfdc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/6/2c6f941fab390e81243e1cd2b40c6178f03ab3f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$220$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />, which gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/c/eec26dec7f825f60497daaca444608ac32f9099e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) } 154}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"73\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28using_the_answer_choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(using_the_answer_choices)\">Solution 3 (using the answer choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (using the answer choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can clearly deduce that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/2/282fdef75f579c92565cd7e0734d83ccfd38bfdc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> of the non-seniors do play an instrument, but, since the total percentage of instrument players is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/8/4282af23ed227721fc5c07c3a27f24991cc4e04a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$46.8\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, the non-senior population is quite low. By intuition, we can therefore see that the answer is around <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/9/09920c3af0daa12ac2ec5174e737c31e0f8cec75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{B}$\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/0/aa04d7a9bcbf1fe3f2037cbc5e763c4b6d2661d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"13\" />. Testing both of these gives us the answer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/c/eec26dec7f825f60497daaca444608ac32f9099e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) } 154}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"73\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/e/f4e4e5c6d549ce47918b94180cad5c1644d9ea88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> of the seniors play a musical instrument, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/e/32e5939a7bdd847ec86582225cd653c240b4abce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> of the non-seniors do not. In addition, we know that the number of people who do not play a musical instrument is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/b/d1ba74ccb0796b66da894348f94b057c6aeaa0ab.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[46.8\\% \\cdot 500 = 46.8 \\cdot 5 = \\frac{468}{2} = 234\\]\" width=\"273\" height=\"37\" />\nWe can also conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/7/fd7edd3842c40dbc1e54e522917a6e07b43c92e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> of the seniors do not play an instrument, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/2/282fdef75f579c92565cd7e0734d83ccfd38bfdc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> of the non seniors do play an instrument, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/b/2ab012be76c47006b6c7ca1fbff265d0aa71f9bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$500-234 = 266$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"130\" height=\"15\" /> people do play an instrument.\n</p><p>We can now set up the following equations, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is the number of seniors and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is the number of non-seniors:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/c/1bc3a4b46bf7b776685a58971584aa2e3edd22fe.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[0.3n + 0.6s = 234\\]\" width=\"139\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/7/b57a3f4d7adffd93a2b18f9a356db07edd498fb6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[0.7n + 0.4s = 266\\]\" width=\"138\" height=\"14\" />\nBy elimination, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/6/0466a37bd0555df5a1d8b0c3dc1a07fe77a3a80f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.5n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"36\" height=\"14\" /> to be equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/e/95e402fe3892da9629b085be0785d4848f5a755a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$330$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />. This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/d/30d6da87ff9c469cc255d5115b5faed7aedf7b2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = \\frac{330}{1.5} = 220$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"120\" height=\"38\" />.\nThe answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/9/aa94edfb9739dcc66dad90f7dd5c148f44a57e2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> percent of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/6/2c6f941fab390e81243e1cd2b40c6178f03ab3f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$220$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />. This is equal to \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/a/94af09c5f582c161f13d632343037e257b9ea43a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[0.7*220 = 7*22 = 154\\]\" width=\"187\" height=\"13\" />\nTherefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/c/eec26dec7f825f60497daaca444608ac32f9099e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) } 154}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"73\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~TheGoldenRetriever\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Faster_Solution_1.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Faster_Solution_1)\">Solution 5 (Faster Solution 1)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Faster Solution 1)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Why don't we consider 100 students first, and multiply by 5 at the end. Then, say there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> seniors and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> non-seniors.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/e/30e4e6cbbd35e2b1d52636a20c0a599ba58abb53.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[s+n = 100\\]\" width=\"92\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/b/bdbb26d91c08c956e8e1ee9063e50b45b40a5ad6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{6}{10}s + \\frac{3}{10}n = 46.8\\]\" width=\"140\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/7/5b78934c6087d3bfac51d24f548e9c74b8bc6189.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies 6s+3n = 468\\]\" width=\"149\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/d/9cd4e62486ff5ab28403bfbfb1125a1767f95479.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies 2s+n = 156\\]\" width=\"140\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>and thus\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/3/fb3a289da25b841b9a7577790a575132d44c4534.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[s = 56, n = 44\\]\" width=\"111\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>We need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/e/44e89248d99363665753d499130fbe0f11793602.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{7}{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> of 5 times this result, meaning we wish to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7cefc9dcbb88bec59db46bf33e2ea1fbb696d90e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22 \\cdot 7 = \\boxed{154}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"105\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/JBZ5AF-dxOc\">https://youtu.be/JBZ5AF-dxOc</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/J8UdaSHyWJI\">https://youtu.be/J8UdaSHyWJI</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution.28Comprehensive.F0.9F.A7.A0.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution(Comprehensive🧠)\">Video Solution(Comprehensive🧠)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution(Comprehensive🧠)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/hO1XW1dlqIE\">https://youtu.be/hO1XW1dlqIE</a>\n</p><p>~Ani_lytical\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B\">2019 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resourc